sprnames[] had no NULL terminator, yet R_InitSpriteDefs counts the sprite
names by scanning for one (as in vanilla linuxdoom, which got away with it
by luck of the link order). Anything non-zero after the table in .data
makes the loader read a garbage name pointer and crash in R_InitSprites;
adding protocol GUIDs to the image did exactly that.

